  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Myanmar project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltspan style=&quot;color: black font-family: Arial, sans-serif&quot;gtThis locally led project addresses urgent EiE, Food Security,&#xa0; Health and&#xa0; Protection/MRE, needs of IDPs and vulnerable groups in 7 Townships (1. Kale, 2. Khin-U, 3. Myaung, 4. Patheingyi, 5. Shwebo, 6. Sintgaing and 7. Taaze of Sagaing regions.&#xa0; Implementation will take place in 50 IDP camps/clusters and host communities with multi-sector interventions targeting areas of greatest need, reaching a total of 34053&#xa0;IDPs and conflict affected people&#xa0; (10,694&#xa0;women, 7,870&#xa0;girls, 7,027&#xa0;boys, 8,462&#xa0;men) including 4768&#xa0;people with disabilities (PWDs). The target areas are affected by the ongoing conflict in Sagaing with the majority of the population displaced and living in makeshift IDP camps in the forest, host communities. This project aims to contribute to the reduction of the immediate suffering of IDPs in these target areas by providing rapid multi-sectoral support, in coordination with other actors working in NW regions and in alignment with the priorities of this allocation.lt/spangtltbrgtlt/pgtltpgtltspan style=&quot;color: black font-family: Arial, sans-serif&quot;gtltbrgtlt/spangtlt/pgtltpgtltspan style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif color: black&quot;gtA conflict-sensitive approach will be followed towards the inclusion of vulnerable people in all project sites. Specific vulnerable groups such as PWDs, People with Specific Needs (PSNs)&#xa0;&#xa0;and female headed households will be prioritized according to cluster/sector guidelines. The project will consider women&#x2019;s specific needs. Gender balanced staff will be recruited where possible, women will be separately engaged in consultations/training and gender dis-aggregated data will be collected. AAP, inclusion and protection, prevention of GBV/SEA, environmental risks, localization and social cohesion will be mainstreamed throughout.lt/spangtlt/pgtltpgtltspan style=&quot;font-family: Arial, sans-serif color: black&quot;gtltbrgtKMSS, CVG (Community Volunteer Group in Myaung) and Health Commission&#xa0;have per-existing and are well positioned to implement this project due to their combined sectoral experience and longstanding presence in the target locations. KMSS is currently implementing humanitarian and development programs in Mandalay and Sagaing region with KMSS staff based in the communities.ltbrgtKMSS will seek the technical support from CRS (Catholic Relief Services) for Cash Based Intervention ( CBI ) as CRS is long term partner in Myanmar and well-known organization in cash based intervention program at global level. ltbrgt
lt/spangtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
